    "node-1yojeld": {
      "supported": false,
      "issue": "The node claims 'Synthetic evaluation record; times and entries reconstructed for exercise.' This is a meta-statement about the evidence packet's nature (stated in incident-description), not an operational fact or condition relevant to the causal chain of the instrument-air interruption. Treating this as a supported 'condition' misclassifies metadata as investigative fact.",
      "evidenceNeeded": "None; reclassify node type from 'condition' to 'meta-note'.",
      "question": ""
    },
    "node-wqqevh": {
      "supported": false,
      "issue": "The claim that P-R normally shows a normal pressure band is an operational assumption not established by the supplied evidence. The shift log (IA-S01) records RHOB's entry 'Morning check: local air indication in normal band' at 08:10 and later entries describing supply complaints, but no source explicitly defines what constitutes the 'normal band' or proves that P-R was within it prior to 10:00 other than operator observation. The node conflates an observed entry with a defined requirement.",
      "evidenceNeeded": "A definition of the normal pressure range for point P-R and evidence establishing whether P-R readings at 09:54–09:59 fell within that range per system specifications, not just operator log entries.",
      "question": "What is the documented normal operating band (in bar gauge) for indication P-R, and does IA-P01 or another source confirm that values of 6.8 bar at 09:54–09:59 were within this band?"
    },
    "node-opiutp": {
      "supported": true,
      "issue": "",
      "evidenceNeeded": "",
      "question": ""
    }
  },"decision":{
"summary":"The causal board contains one meta-node (node-1yojeld) that should be reclassified and two condition nodes where evidence gaps exist. Node-wqqevh relies on an unverified assumption about the 'normal band' without a defined threshold or specification; node-opiutp is supported by explicit text in IA-D01.","evidenceUsed":["incident-description","b678a928-a8d2-472d-bc03-2e1a3dc411e6#1","24ec1587-92e9-4320-82c2-30368d834f1d"],"unknowns":["Exact normal pressure band for P-R (if any) and whether 6.8 bar qualifies as 'normal' per system specs.","Whether the air interruption originated upstream, downstream, or in distribution remains unknown due to lack of valve-state data."],"alternatives":["The low-pressure alarm may have been triggered by a transient leak that self-sealed before restoration at 10:07; this is plausible but unproven without continuous waveform data.","A maintenance-related valve misconfiguration during boundary preparation could have caused the drop, but no evidence of such action exists yet."],"confidence":0.85}
}
